25:T4a3,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is there to see in AlUla?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The highlights are Hegra (Mada'in Salih), a UNESCO World Heritage Site with 111 Nabataean tombs, the ancient city of Dadan, the inscriptions at Jabal Ikmah, and the natural Elephant Rock formation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When is the best time to visit AlUla?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"October to March, when daytime temperatures are a comfortable 15–25°C. Summers regularly exceed 40°C and are best avoided for outdoor sightseeing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I get to AlUla?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You can fly directly into AlUla (ULH) Airport from Riyadh or Jeddah, or take a premium road transfer — roughly 10 hours from Riyadh or around 3 hours from Madinah."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I get around AlUla's attractions?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The sites are spread across the valley, so a private car or guided transfer is the most comfortable way to link Hegra, Dadan, Jabal Ikmah, and the resorts at your own pace."}}]}1a:["$","div",null,{"className":"min-h-screen bg-[#FAFAF7] text-[#1C1C1C] pb-24","children":[[["$","script","0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Article\",\"headline\":\"AlUla Visitor Guide — Hegra, Dadan & the Rose City\",\"description\":\"What to see in AlUla — Hegra's 111 Nabataean tombs, Dadan, Jabal Ikmah and Elephant Rock — the best season to visit (October to March), and how far apart the sites are.\",\"url\":\"https://taxisaudiarabia.com/guides/alula-transport-guide\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://taxisaudiarabia.com/guides/alula-transport-guide\"},\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Taxi Saudi Arabia\",\"url\":\"https://taxisaudiarabia.com/about\"},\"publisher\":{\